+# smallpt — a little light experiment
+
+Kevin Beason's MIT-licensed C++ smallpt integrator, compiled to WebAssembly.
+Open index.html through your static web host. The page needs HTTP(S), because
+module workers and WebAssembly loading are restricted on file:// URLs.
+
+The renderer runs entirely in a dedicated module worker. Randomize colors,
+change either material, pick sample count/resolution, reset, or download a PNG.
+Changing a setting cancels the preceding worker. Rows are transferred as RGBA
+buffers; neither scene data nor pixels are uploaded.
+
+## Rebuild
+Requires Emscripten (em++ on PATH) and Node.js for the optional preview build.
+
+- npm run build — compile assets/smallpt.mjs and assets/smallpt.wasm.
+- npm run build:preview — render assets/preview.png using the compiled Wasm in
+  Node.js (720×540, 256 spp). This may take a few minutes.
+
+The generated artifacts are checked in, so a static host needs no compiler.
+No development server or browser verification was used.
+
+## Source and modifications
+Original: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/
+Original source: src/smallpt-original.cpp
+Adaptation: src/smallpt.cpp
+License: src/LICENSE.txt
+
+The original radiance integrator and Cornell-box sphere geometry are retained.
+The browser adaptation replaces the CLI/PPM main with bounded row rendering,
+adds material/color setters and an RGBA buffer, neutralizes the wall colors,
+and limits recursion to 128 bounces to bound stack usage. The initial scene
+uses a terracotta diffuse sphere and warm glass sphere.
